{
  "dom_id": "step-q106247",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14244048/assets/3f07f2e5473df35b47f3033428fee4ae9b38cf554c00f0ddd1cb12a40d981710.png)\n\nFind the minimum value of the parabola $y=(x+1)^{2}+5$, sketched above.",
  "worked_solution": "The minimum value of the parabola is the $y$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola. \n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=(x+1)^{2}+5\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-1$ and $k=5.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-1,5),$ and its minimum value is $5.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
